/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A PV cell is a current source in parallel with a diode; sunlight sets the current.
   - Irradiance moves current almost in proportion.
   - Perturb and observe (P&O): measure V and I, compute P, step the boost duty, measure again, compare.
   - Two arrangements: two-stage has a boost MPPT stage onto a DC bus plus a separate inverter; single-stage lets the inverter do MPPT and accept a wider input window.
   - Hysteresis control makes inverter current follow a sine.
   - fs = (Vdc² − vg²) / (2 h L Vdc)
   - fs is switching frequency in Hz; Vdc the DC bus voltage in volts; vg the instantaneous grid voltage in volts; h the hysteresis band in amperes; L the filter inductance in henries.
   - The switching frequency varies: highest near vg = 0, lowest near the sine peak.
   - Model the inverter as sinusoidal source E behind coupling reactance X feeding stiff grid V.
   - P = (E V / X) sin δ Q = (E V cos δ − V²) / X
*/
