/* book exam traps: Controller output is not the firing angle: 50 % output is α = 90° on a phase-angle controller but a 50 % duty cycle on an integral-cycle one. | Heater power follows RMS current, P = Irms²R, not average current. | On a 4–20 mA loop, 4 mA is the 0 % reading of the scale; a 0 mA reading means a broken loop. | Integral-cycle control avoids switching harmonics, but its bursts still thermal-cycle the element if the period is long and can flicker lamps on the same supply. */
